  <prompt>
    Implement FR-03 + FR-05: a NEW adapter in `Services/Compose/` that runs the `Docxodus`
    `WmlComparer` (7.1.0, MIT — added by task 001) between the retained load-time original `.docx` and
    the spliced-edited document produced by task 020, synthesizing the minimal `w:ins`/`w:del` revision
    markup and persisting the comparison output. Set author attribution on the emitted revisions.
    Inline run-formatting edits (bold/italic/font) inside a changed paragraph MUST be represented via
    WmlComparer's Format-Change Detection (`rPr`/`pPrChange`), NOT as a full-run delete+re-insert
    (FR-05 / D4). The adapter MUST NOT throw on the S1/S1b edge cases: nested tables, multi-level
    numbering, whole-paragraph delete, paragraph split. This task builds + unit-proves the comparer
    adapter in isolation; wiring it into the inverted `SaveAsync` is task 022.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 developer fluent in the Microsoft Open XML SDK 3.x and the Docxodus / Open-Xml-
    PowerTools `WmlComparer` API surface (compare two `WmlDocument`s → revision-marked output;
    `WmlComparerSettings` incl. author attribution; Format-Change + Move detection). Understands the
    packaging constraint: the diff path must stay off `HtmlToWml`/`FormattingAssembler` so SkiaSharp is
    never re-pulled (the SkiaSharp assets are excluded by task 001).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A NEW adapter service in `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/` that wraps Docxodus
    `WmlComparer`: given the retained-original bytes and the spliced-edited bytes (task 020 output), it
    returns the redline-marked `.docx` bytes carrying minimal `w:ins`/`w:del` with author attribution,
    and inline run-format edits represented as `rPr`/`pPrChange` (not del+ins). Matching unit tests in
    `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/` assert: 3 edited paragraphs → minimal ins/del;
    author attribution present; bolding a word yields a format-change (not a full-run del+ins); no
    exception on nested-table / numbering / delete / split fixtures (S1/S1b).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §4.2 (Docxodus `WmlComparer` is the paragraph-redline engine — off-the-shelf MIT, adopted
      not hand-written), §8 (SAVE pipeline: "Docxodus WmlComparer → minimal w:ins/w:del (+move/format)"),
      §12 bullet 3 (packaging: exclude SkiaSharp; NEVER touch `HtmlToWml`/`FormattingAssembler`). S1
      proved WmlComparer preserves paraIds on unchanged paragraphs, emits minimal ins/del, and detects
      format changes; S1b hardened it on nested tables, 3-level numbering, delete, and split. S3 proved
      the managed diff runs with SkiaSharp fully removed (net add ≈ 2.44 MB). The comparer re-serializes
      (cosmetic BOM/whitespace) — the fidelity claim is structural/semantic (Approach A), not byte-identity.
    </background>
