  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-03">Run `Docxodus` `WmlComparer` (7.1.0, MIT) between the retained original and the spliced-edited document to synthesize minimal `w:ins`/`w:del`; set author attribution; persist the comparison output. No exception on nested tables / numbering / delete / split (S1/S1b).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-05 / D4">Inline run-formatting edits (bold/italic/font) inside a changed paragraph MUST be represented via WmlComparer Format-Change Detection (`rPr`/`pPrChange`), NOT a full-run delete+re-insert.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / design §12 bullet 3">MUST NOT invoke Docxodus `HtmlToWml` or `FormattingAssembler` on any code path — either re-pulls SkiaSharp and breaks the packaging exclusion. The diff path uses `WmlComparer` only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 / ADR-029 / CLAUDE.md §10">Measure BFF publish size after this task's code lands; report absolute compressed + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (state PDB convention). Docxodus net add ≈ 2.44 MB managed (~1 MB compressed) with SkiaSharp excluded — verify the exclusion still holds at publish time (no `libSkiaSharp` in output). ≤60 MB ceiling; ≥+5 MB single-task → justify.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02 / NFR-03">No new HIGH CVE from the Docxodus + OpenXml 3.5.1 additions (`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`). Permissive licenses only (Docxodus MIT) — no AGPL.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Byte-stream operation only; no `Microsoft.Graph` types in `Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">The adapter MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`, executor, or routing types; Tier-1 NetArchTest enforces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Unit tests use real `.docx` fixtures + the S1/S1b edge-case docs; mock only at the SpeFileStore facade if any I/O is exercised. NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration/ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State the Placement Justification for the new adapter in the PR description, citing `bff-extensions.md`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

