  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + dependency check">Confirm task 001 (Docxodus present, SkiaSharp excluded) + task 020 (spliced-edited output) are available. Output the FULL rigor-level declaration. Read the S1/S1b spike notes for the validated comparer recipe. Load knowledge files + bff-extensions.md; state the Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Design the adapter surface">Define the adapter contract: (retained-original bytes, spliced-edited bytes, author) → redline-marked bytes. Keep the DTO in `Services/Compose/`. Confirm the WmlComparer call path touches no `HtmlToWml`/`FormattingAssembler`.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Implement the WmlComparer adapter">Wrap `WmlComparer.Compare` (or the S1-validated entry point): load both docs as `WmlDocument`, set `WmlComparerSettings` author attribution, run the compare, return the revision-marked bytes. Ensure Format-Change Detection is enabled so run-format edits emit `rPr`/`pPrChange` not del+ins. Persist/return the comparison output.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Unit tests (incl. S1/S1b edge cases)">Author tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/`: 3 edited paragraphs → minimal ins/del + author attribution set; bolding a word → a format-change (`rPr`/`pPrChange`), asserted NOT a full-run del+ins; no exception on nested-table, 3-level-numbering, whole-paragraph delete, and paragraph-split fixtures.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify + size/CVE report">Build BFF + run tests. Publish + verify no `libSkiaSharp` in output; report absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable` — no new HIGH CVE. Tier-1 NetArchTest facade check. Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ (NEW WmlComparer adapter + DTO)</output>
