  </outputs>

  <justification>
    <existing>No in-repo component synthesizes minimal `w:ins`/`w:del` by diffing two whole documents. `DocxAnnotationWriter` writes caller-supplied redline/comment markup (it does not diff); no other `Services/Compose/` service compares documents. Verified by Grep.</existing>
    <extension>The closest existing (`DocxAnnotationWriter`) covers only the AI-redline authoring subset (design §11) — it cannot compute the direct-typing paragraph delta. Rather than hand-write a paragraph-diff algorithm (historically hard), R3 adopts the maintained off-the-shelf MIT engine `Docxodus WmlComparer` (design §11 Path C — dependency adoption, not net-new code). The only new *code* is the thin adapter wrapping it.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the comparer adapter, direct-typing edits cannot be turned into minimal tracked-change markup on the retained-original baseline — FR-03/FR-05 acceptance (minimal ins/del; format-change not del+ins) and the E1 delta save cannot be met; dirty saves stay lossy.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Running the adapter on the retained original + a spliced-edited doc with 3 edited paragraphs yields minimal `w:ins`/`w:del` (not a whole-body rewrite), with author attribution set on the emitted revisions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Bolding a word inside a changed paragraph yields an `rPr`/`pPrChange` (Format-Change Detection), asserted NOT to be a full-run del+ins (FR-05 / D4).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The adapter throws no exception on the S1/S1b edge-case fixtures: nested tables, 3-level numbering, whole-paragraph delete, paragraph split.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No code path invokes Docxodus `HtmlToWml` or `FormattingAssembler`; the published output contains no `libSkiaSharp` native asset.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB (Docxodus net ≈ 2.44 MB managed, SkiaSharp excluded); no new HIGH CVE; only MIT deps.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (Tier-1 NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Matching unit tests exist and pass; BFF build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
