  <notes>
    COMPLETE 2026-07-17 (opus @ xhigh, FULL rigor, directional).

    NEW `Services/Compose/ComposeRedlineComparerService.cs` — thin Docxodus WmlComparer adapter:
    `byte[] SynthesizeRedline(ReadOnlyMemory&lt;byte&gt; retainedOriginal, ReadOnlyMemory&lt;byte&gt;
    splicedEdited, string author, DateTimeOffset? revisionTimestamp = null)`. Mirrors the
    DocxAnnotationWriter byte-in/byte-out shape. NEW `ComposeRedlineException`. DI: unconditional
    singleton in ComposeModule (symmetric per bff-extensions.md §F.1).

    §6.5 Path-C (API-shape delta from S1 recipe, NON-blocking — same fork lineage): S1 validated on
    Docxodus 7.1.0 (net10); task 001 shipped 6.4.0 (net8). Verified the 6.4.0 public surface by
    reflection FIRST: `WmlComparer.Compare(WmlDocument, WmlDocument, WmlComparerSettings)` identical;
    byte-in ctor is `WmlDocument(string fileName, byte[])` (NOT bare `(byte[])` — used a synthetic
    "original.docx"/"edited.docx" name to satisfy its extension sniff); output via
    `WmlDocument.DocumentByteArray`; format-change is the explicit `WmlComparerSettings.DetectFormatChanges`
    bool (set true for FR-05); author via `AuthorForRevisions`, date via `DateTimeForRevisions`.

    Diff path = WmlComparer ONLY — no HtmlToWml/FormattingAssembler (design §12 bullet 3); publish
    verified 0 libSkiaSharp assets, Docxodus.dll present (MIT).

    Tests: NEW ComposeRedlineComparerServiceTests (12) — text edits produce ins/del + single author
    attribution; untouched paras keep w14:paraId + carry no revisions (minimal, S1); identical docs →
    0 revisions; bold-a-word → rPr/pPrChange asserted NOT del+ins (FR-05/D4, DeletedText never contains
    the reformatted word); S1/S1b no-throw on nested tables (2 tables survive) / 3-level numbering /
    whole-para delete (→ w:del) / paragraph split; empty/whitespace/malformed → ArgumentException /
    ComposeRedlineException. Text-edit fixtures produced through ComposeParagraphSpliceService (task 020)
    so the tests exercise the real 020→021 pipeline. Fixtures include a StyleDefinitionsPart (WmlComparer
    reads it via AddFootnotesEndnotesStyles — real Word docs always have one).

    Gates: Compose suite 429 ✅ (+12); ADR013_ComposeFacade PASS; publish 45.94 MB compressed incl PDBs
    (0 delta vs 012/020 — Docxodus counted since task 001), ≤60 MB; 0 vulnerable packages; ADR-007 no
    Graph type; ADR-010 concrete singleton. §9.5 code-review + adr-check PASS. PR MUST include §10
    Placement Justification (new adapter; §11 justified — no existing component diffs two whole docs;
    DocxAnnotationWriter writes caller-supplied markup, does not diff).

    Consumed by task 022 (SaveAsync inversion — NOT wired here). NFR-06 seam obligation rides task 022.
  </notes>
</task>
